# `fluid::TimeControl`

An action that fires at a given second of the run.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::TimeControl
```

## What It Does

Applies an `Action` at an exact elapsed time. The hydraulic clock lands on `at`, so the change takes effect at that second.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `at` | Seconds from the start of the run. | 0 |
| `action` | The `Action` to apply. |  |

## Returns

A value; carried by `Schedule::time`.

## Errors

A time outside the run interval is rejected by `run`.

## Interpretation and Use

Use a time control for a known program, an off-peak tariff or a flushing sequence. The action persists after it fires.

